## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — viewer must not obscure, truncate, or misrepresent document content; all pages must be accessible
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — viewer failures (failed to render, missing pages) must fail closed with explicit error; never silently show partial content as complete

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-011:** Clinician or administrator misses content on a multi-page document due to poor pagination or scroll behaviour — clinical action taken on incomplete information
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-012:** Document rendered incorrectly (wrong orientation, truncated content) — misread or missed clinical information
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

- **HAZ-DOC-013:** Viewer silently fails to render all pages — user believes document is single-page when it is not
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-010:** Page count displayed explicitly in viewer (e.g. "Page 2 of 7") so user always knows total page count
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-011:** Rotation controls available for scanned documents to correct orientation before review
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-012:** If viewer fails to render any page, explicit error shown for that page; total page count still displayed so user knows content is missing
  - **Type:** Error Handling
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

